# Tooling

Python 3.12. Stack: uv, FastAPI, uvicorn, SQLModel, Typer, Rich, pytest, ruff, SQLite.

## uv only

Every Python, install, and test command goes through `uv`. Never `pip`, never bare `python` / `pytest` / `ruff`.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
pip install fastapi
python -m pytest
ruff check .

# ✅ GOOD
uv add fastapi
uv add --dev pytest ruff
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check
uv run ruff format --check
uv run uvicorn atlas.api.app:app --reload
```

Use `uv add` / `uv add --dev` / `uv sync`. The lockfile is `uv.lock`; do not invent a `requirements.txt`.

## Pre-commit gates

Before every commit, all must pass:

1. `uv run ruff check`
2. `uv run ruff format --check`
3. `uv run pytest`

A finding is work: apply `ruff check --fix` / `ruff format` when the tool can, then inspect the rest. See `.cursor/rules/checks.mdc`. Do not commit with a known failure.

## Frontend (`web/`)

pnpm and Biome only. See `.cursor/rules/frontend.mdc`. Never `npm` / `yarn` / ESLint / Prettier / oxlint in `web/`.


